    "summary": "The trade buys 300 EBL at Tk 26.6, raising EBL weight to 6.35% and Bank sector weight to 24.86% (target 25%), while Pharmaceuticals & Chemicals falls to 37.3% (target 30%) and SQURPHARMA falls to 25.12% (limit 25%). Existing rule violations persist with no new ones created. The trade matches journal theses j-027, j-018, and j-006, supporting the direction of adding a cheap second bank to spread exposure beyond BRACBANK.",
    "review_markdown": "- EBL weight increases from 5.15% to 6.35%; Bank sector weight rises from 23.89% to 24.86% (target 25%). Pharmaceuticals & Chemicals weight falls from 37.78% to 37.3% (target 30%). SQURPHARMA weight falls from 25.44% to 25.12% (limit 25%). Telecommunication weight falls from 15.58% to 15.39% (target 15%). Fuel & Power weight falls from 9.16% to 9.05% (target 10%). Food & Allied weight falls from 9.09% to 8.98% (target 10%). Cement weight falls from 4.5% to 4.44% (target 5%). [q:6fa42096-3acf-4f27-8eb2-c1e707f5b8ae]\n- Commission cost is 31.92 BDT on a gross purchase of 7,980 BDT, raising total market value from 631,708.80 BDT to 639,838.80 BDT. [q:6fa42096-3acf-4f27-8eb2-c1e707f5b8ae]\n- The trade does not create new rule findings; the existing violations (Pharmaceuticals & Chemicals at 37.8% vs 30% target, SQURPHARMA at 25.4% vs 25% limit) persist. [q:87556351-208a-4f07-9ec7-bbb18ae0387b]\n- The trade matches three journal theses: j-027 and j-018 (adding to EBL at a low price against book value) and j-006 (a cheap second bank to spread bank exposure beyond BRACBANK). [q:6fa42096-3acf-4f27-8eb2-c1e707f5b8ae]\n\n**What I remembered**\n- Week to 2026-09-17: no rule broken; EBL rose 6.2%, the largest move. [q:mem-54]\n\n**What to look at next**\n- Pharmaceuticals & Chemicals sector target; the portfolio's weight after this trade.\n\nNot covered: announcements between 2026-09-01 and 2026-10-01 for EBL; no rows were returned.\n\nThis is a review of your own records, not financial advice.",
